@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-03
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, commit 3556e27, commit 2b56ba7, claude/hooks/conductor-gate.sh]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh
+---
+# 0012: Keep a small conductor gate; trim it, do not replace it
+
+**Context.** "#4b" asked to replace the 552-line gate with `permissions` rules and a ~50-line gate ([gate-shrink-detail](../../../.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md) §1). Replaying 881 conductor Bash calls from 8 transcripts (2026-10-18..28) through the gate gave 754 allowed (§3). Never used: `git show --stat`, `herdr status|pane list|layout|workspace|tab`, `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse|pr status`, jq as a pipe consumer (0 allowed). Chaining with `;`/`&` was 5.8% of allowed calls and pipes 0. A B′ spike (native subagents instead of the harness runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 ([RESULTS](../../../.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md)): subagents die when the conductor exits ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so the detached runner, and the gate that fences the conductor, stay.
+
+**Decision.** Trim the gate to observed use; keep it as a script.
+- Removed (earlier steps, commit 3556e27 and the v21 single-command scanner): jq segment checks, `git show`, `git_branch_ok` (now a list-only regex: `-a -r -v --show-current`), herdr beyond `pane get|current`, gh beyond `pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge`, the explicit Agent/Workflow/Monitor/NotebookEdit deny cases and the `mcp__filesystem__*` block (the tools are in `conductor.md` `disallowedTools`; the hook MATCHER is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`), the segment splitter (one command per call).
+- Policy tables (messages, `BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY`) sit in one block after the prologue.
+- Prune step 5 adds one gate test per form under "You may run directly" in `conductor.md`, and `tests/gate-denied.list` keeps every probe denied.
+- Kept: the path helpers (`rel`/`physrel`/`physical`, readable/writable, raw-stream rule) and the Bash allowlist. `permissions` rules cannot resolve symlinks or keep `.harness/log/*.jsonl` unreadable, and a regex over a command string is not a shell scanner.
+- Option f, `permissions` rules in place of the gate, is rejected: user-scope rules bind workers too, and workers must read and write source. A per-repo rule set would need the same checkout opt-in the gate already has ([0010](0010-herdr-optional-gate-by-checkout.md)).
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the 4b consequence in [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md) ("a separate design"). Gate 552 → 513 lines.
+
+**Consequences.** A new conductor need (another gh subcommand, `git show`) is a deliberate edit of one table plus a test, not a loosening by accident. The gate is still a live file: follow [live-gate-edit](../troubleshooting/live-gate-edit.md). `--via` was removed in the same step (commit 2b56ba7), so `harness ask` refuses it as an unknown option.
